## Required outputs

Write a file only for a changed block:

| block | path |
|---|---|
| new skill | `{{ output_folder }}/skills/create/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` |
| deployed skill revision | `{{ output_folder }}/skills/update/<existing-skill-name>/SKILL.md` |
| system prompt | `{{ output_folder }}/system_prompt/optimized_prompt.yaml` |
| tool descriptions | `{{ output_folder }}/tool_descriptions/optimized_tool_descriptions.yaml` |

A skill uses the existing name when updated and has this form:

```markdown
---
name: <skill-name>
description: "Use when <recognizable task or conversation condition>. <Purpose>."
---

# <Title>

<optional short overview for a comprehensive skill>

## Workflow
<finding-backed executable steps>

## Decision Rules
<optional finding-backed branches, priorities, and stopping conditions>

## Common Mistakes
<optional recurring mistakes directly supported by findings>

## Rules and Constraints
<optional finding-backed domain facts required to execute the workflow>
```

`## Workflow` is required. The other body sections are optional; omit any that would be
empty or duplicate another section. Do not add a body-level `## When to Use` section:
encode the complete loading trigger in the frontmatter `description`.

The system-prompt artifact contains the complete copied prompt:

```yaml
system_prompt: |
  <complete prompt with surgical edits>
```

The tool-description artifact contains complete replacements for edited tools only:

```yaml
tool_descriptions:
  <tool_name>: |
    <complete replacement description>
```

Always write `{{ output_folder }}/findings.json`. Include every admitted finding, including
findings assigned to `none`; use an empty array when no finding is admitted:

```json
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "f01",
      "statement": "<one imperative sentence>",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "trace": "<filename>.json",
          "message_index": 9,
          "claim": "<what this trajectory message directly shows>"
        },
        {
          "trace": "<filename>.json",
          "evaluator_result": "failure|pass",
          "evaluator_index": 0,
          "claim": "<what this evaluator explanation establishes>"
        },
        "skill:<name>#<distinct supplied text>",
        "system_prompt:<distinct supplied text>",
        "tool_description:<tool>#<distinct supplied text>"
      ],
      "polarity": "worked|failed",
      "situation": "<recognizable task or conversation condition>|any task",
      "miss_cost": "violated|slower",
      "already_present_in": ["<skill:name|system_prompt|tool_description:name>"],
      "targets": ["<selected objective term>"],
      "destination": {
        "block": "skill|system_prompt|tool_description|none",
        "name": "<skill name|tool name|system_prompt|null>"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Evidence indices are zero-based. Each structured evidence object uses either
`message_index` or `evaluator_result` with `evaluator_index`. Use separate message objects
when a claim depends on both a call and its result. Add `destination.tool_aspect` only for
a tool-description finding. Add `rationale` only when the destination is `none` or existing
guidance is relocated.

Reconcile all candidates before writing, inspect the completed artifacts against
`findings.json`, fix unsupported or misplaced changes, and then stop.
